id: pm-context-acquisition-boundary
title: Reject sparse evidence acquisition contracts before planning
description: Revalidate the shipped next-evidence planner against the refreshed backlog contract; fix sparse SDK arrays and unbounded prevalidation serialization without duplicating PR 176 or PR 183.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: next-evidence,validation
created_at: "2026-10-28T19:44:44.590Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T20:07:36.575Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Three overlapping reads select the cheapest complete cover or disclose uncovered criteria; no read executes; revised source contracts invalidate saved plans.; A single bounded dense packet schema is shared by SDK planning and CLI validation; sparse and extreme inputs refuse with typed remedies before planning; previously valid packets and JSON/TOON plans remain compatible.; At least 500 seeded operation sequences verify exact cover decisions, older-input replays, CRLF variants, serialization and SDK-read native state including relationships; public tracker copy is unchanged and measured.; Packed installation paths and targeted local checks pass; exact-head CI npm and Bun release gates pass at unchanged thresholds."
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T19:45:31.186Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked at main 0a8e1db: SDK packContextCandidates packs ranked present candidates under a token budget; pm-context evidence-packing.ts binds existing tracker fields. Acquisition planning already shipped in PR 176 (pm-context-next-evidence), with JSON estimate repair PR 183. Reuse those exports and context-next-evidence, not a duplicate planner. pm-ops diagnostic-plans.ts executes reviewed diagnostics; pm-rlm adaptive.ts owns model-driven decomposition. New reproduced defect: sparse missing/covers arrays pass the SDK parser and emit null IDs. Plan: enforce bounded dense schema before serialization, share the planner validation boundary with CLI, preserve valid v1 contracts, add property/refusal/compatibility/revert tests and refresh public-data plus packed acceptance."
  "2026-10-28T19:52:39.487Z",codex-agent,"Implemented bounded own-element array checks before cloning or serialization; CLI delegates raw JSON once to the same SDK parser. Revised public SDK signatures accept unknown at the validated boundary. Released-v1 fixture preserves original digest and plan. New refusal corpus covers every sparse location, inherited elements, maximum-length arrays and serialization hooks; 500 additional seeded mutations cover extreme numbers. Behavioral revert in a disposable copy: replacing only parseNextEvidencePacket with main and rebuilding makes the dense-schema regression fail (1 failed); restoring and rebuilding passes (1 passed). Refreshed public main 0a8e1db snapshot: 97 items, 36 with criteria/tests; 3 catalog reads selects 1; 7 missing criteria, 6 covered, 1 disclosed gap; estimated tokens 523, calls 1, cost 563 versus alternative 915; JSON 869 bytes, TOON 912 bytes; zero reads executed, unchanged tracker fingerprint. Typecheck and docstring lint pass. Initial focused suite exposed a test-only nonconfigurable hook; corrected and its three focused tests pass; complete focused rerun follows."
  "2026-10-28T19:54:40.706Z",codex-agent,"Local strict health has a pre-existing ignored extension skew (pinned host 2026.10.25 versus locally installed pm-github 2026.10.28); history drift passes and other provenance/staleness findings are advisory. CI uses a clean checkout without ignored extensions. No extension, telemetry or existing history was changed; existing pm-context-595f tracks tracker-health work."
  "2026-10-28T19:58:05.436Z",codex-agent,"Linked targeted test ran through pm test --run --progress: 12/12 passed, zero skips/failures; next-evidence.ts measured 100% lines, branches and functions. Includes 500 SDK-read state sequences (2000 operations), 500 numeric producer/transport cases, 500 invalid-boundary mutations, no-git installed CLI and five peer-transition boundaries. Native test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment records the execution receipt without changing that policy."
  "2026-10-28T20:00:55.434Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance runner now installs the captured archive through supported pm package install, as recommended by the host. Directory installs omit external dependencies and can fail module activation; archive installation prepares those dependencies and a direct archive probe activated all ten package commands successfully. This is an installation-route correction, not a planner or SDK acquisition workaround. Revision string bounds are also checked before trim to bound validation work; the focused boundary checks are rerunning after this small change."
  "2026-10-28T20:07:31.943Z",codex-agent,"Final local acceptance: all six captured-artifact launchers pass (npm project-local, Bun project-local, npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx), 24/24 assertions for compact JSON, saved-plan revalidation, SDK-decoded TOON and unchanged artifact digest. Host pin 2026.10.25. Archive: 49 entries, 132924 packed bytes, 577320 unpacked bytes; SHA-256 bd0cc81102dd6cb248d7ac29a1972e5d7d63a974d3a4c974d81c87782045ad9e. After the final revision-length ordering change, boundary subset 5/5, source/test typechecks and docstring lint pass. Full targeted linked test previously passed 12/12 with 100/100/100 scoped coverage; complete npm and Bun release gates are delegated to exact-head CI at unchanged thresholds. Changelog generation/check pass with no diff. Final CI URL/counts will be reported on the PR and in the final report; no tracker writes are planned after final-head CI verification. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification; releasing only this author claim."
